<p>With <a href="https://www.britishmuseum.org/exhibitions/bayeux-tapestry">the Bayeux Tapestry now on display at the British Museum</a>,<em> <a href="https://www.britishmuseum.org/exhibitions/bayeux-tapestry">Deep Down History</a> </em>presents a deep dive into the embroidery’s full story:</p>
<p>“The Bayeux Tapestry is one of the most remarkable survivals of the Middle Ages — a 70 metre embroidered account of the events leading to the Norman Conquest of England in 1066, culminating in the Battle of Hastings. This video tells the Tapestry’s story in full, using Charles Stothard’s early colour reproduction, presented here as a seamless scroll for the first time. We follow Harold Godwinson’s fateful journey from Edward the Confessor’s court to Normandy, his later seizure of the Crown, and William the Conqueror’s invasion. Beyond its political messaging, the Tapestry is also bursting with medieval history, including jokes, fascinating technical details, and a warning for those who break their promises…”</p>
